      "evidence_id": "E1"
     },
     {
      "text": "100%",
      "value": 100.0,
      "evidence_id": "E1"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "The positive correlation reflects a common time trend on waterflood, not choke driving water: the well was already above the 80% design limit from Feb 2012 and oil fell as water took liquid capacity.",
    "detail": "E2: 30-day median water_cut first above 0.80 on 2012-02-14. E3 shows WOR rising from 2.6 in 2011-01 to 17.78 in 2013-12 while liquid flat and choke 98-100%. Field voidage replacement near 1.02-1.03 in 2011-2013, so injection sustained pressure.",
    "evidence_ids": [
     "E2",
     "E3"
    ],
    "confidence": "inference",
    "numbers": [
     {
      "text": "80%",
      "value": 0.8,
